        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "p",
         "text": "Why it matters",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "h2",
         "text": "What Makes a Strong Contractor Logo?",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<p>A strong contractor logo is simple, heavy enough to read from across a job site and specific enough that people remember your name. Homeowners in Austin see dozens of trucks every week. The ones that stick have a clear name, one confident symbol and colors that do not fade into the background.</p><p>Construction logos also take a beating. They get cut from vinyl, screen printed on shirts, stamped on hard hats and shrunk onto bid packets. We design with those uses in mind: thick strokes, limited colors, and a one-color version that still works on a white truck or a black trailer.</p>",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "list",
         "items": [
          {
           "text": "A clear name that reads from the street",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "One or two colors that print and cut cleanly",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "Versions for light and dark trucks, signs and gear",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          }
         ],
         "classes": []
        }
       ]
      },
